<title>GERMANY: Hoechst - 96 dividend won't disappoint.</title>
<headline>Hoechst - 96 dividend won't disappoint.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and drugs group Hoechst AG said on Wednesday that it would not disappoint shareholders with its 1996 dividend payout, even though a decision has not yet been taken on the amount.</p>
<p>&quot;A decision on the dividend has not been taken, but it won't be lower and the shareholders will not be disappointed, &quot; said Hoechst chief financial officer Klaus Schmieder at a news conference.</p>
<p>On 1995 earnings the company paid a 13 mark ($8.52) dividend.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.525 German Marks)</p>
